# Whitelist: everything is excluded, then the files meant to be public are let
# back in. An mpv config folder fills up with private files like the watch
# history, so a blacklist here would be one forgotten rule away from leaking.
*
!*/

!.gitignore
!.luacheckrc
!LICENSE
!*.md
!mpv.conf
!input.conf
!script-opts/*.conf
!scripts/**/*.lua
!tests/*.lua
!docs/images/*.png
!.github/workflows/*.yml
!tools/*.py
!tools/mdi/*.svg
!tools/mdi/LICENSE

# Backstop: these win over the rules above, so private files can never be
# committed. They are anchored to the config folder itself -- without the
# leading / they would also swallow scripts/boda/mod/history.lua.
/history.*
/bookmarks.*
/recent-folders.*
/ui-state.*
/skip-map.*
/watch_later/
/cache/
*.log
*.pid
*.bgra
*.m3u
*.m3u8
